The score-generation and radix-selection kernels in cute_score.py,
cute_score_generic.py, cute_topk.py and cute_topk_gvr2.py adapt cuDNN Frontend source at commit
1ab7d63be81f1ef2eb3b2dea5367219cf9674a5f. Attention Gym changes their interfaces,
workspace layout, scheduling and outputs; they do not depend on the cuDNN
Frontend package. The applicable license is in LICENSE.Apache-2.0.

cute_score_mxfp8.py adapts the same score pipeline and the scale-copy partition
from CUTLASS's dense_blockscaled_gemm_persistent.py example. The applicable
BSD-3-Clause terms for that partition are reproduced in cute_score_mxfp8.py.

cute_topk_gvr2.py adapts the streaming main-family algorithm and float4 load
helper from FlashInfer's topk_varlen/kernels/gvr2_topk_decode.py at commit
c11c1090172f578bad37b8bca2b40e4161d72144 (derived from TensorRT-LLM PR #17821,
ed94d4cfbf), Copyright (c) 2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION. All rights reserved.
The applicable Apache-2.0 terms are in LICENSE.Apache-2.0. Attention Gym changes
the interface, finite-score arithmetic, scratch ownership, exact refinement,
and fallback behavior; it does not port the other three kernel families.
triton_gvr2.py is independently implemented from the same GVR2 algorithm.
Neither selector introduces a FlashInfer runtime dependency.

